Z||000000||fierocd||04-09-2001||05:15 PM||||I am fixing my 86 gt and I am taking most of the parts I need of my 86 se that I recently crashed.  My question is, I have 2 engine, both run well, but what is the best/easiest way to figure out which one is mechanically better.  I just bought a new compression gauge and plan on checking that on both tuesday or wednesday.  Is there anything else that would help me decide.  Even if I don't switch engines, the gt will be getting a new clutch.(I replaced the one in the se 4 days before I crashed it) any ideas are helpfull, thanks.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Carrolles||04-09-2001||05:49 PM||||compare the mileage of both.<BR>how does the oil look?<BR>vacuum harness?<BR>egr tube?<BR>harmonic damper - is the center part separating from the outer ring, does the rubber material between the two parts look dry and cracked?<BR>exhaust manifold leaks?<BR>thermostat housing look ok?<P>What a problem.  You have two good motors and one good car.  I have two good cars and one good motor.||||reg||1
Z||000002||fierocd||04-09-2001||05:56 PM||||Milage doesn't matter-both cars reconstruted titles(don't know actual milage)<BR>oil looks fine in both-no metal or signs of contamination<BR>vacume harness-looks good on both<BR>egr tube-just bought new one with new egr valve<BR>harmonic damper-??? don't know<BR>exhaust manifold gaskets are getting changed<BR>thermostat housing looks fine on both<P>actually, I have 3 fieros-2 good bodies, 3 good engines||||reg||1
